A dry run reports what it would do and writes nothing.

```
$ jci-coverage complexity --dry-run
[..]INFO jci_coverage::complexity: complexity [..]
[..]WARN jci_coverage::complexity: no matching function in the source [..]
complexity: 4 methods in the report, 3 after merging 1 duplicate instantiation(s)
  2 matched, 1 not matched to a source function
  total 5, mean 1.67, max 4
  most complex:
       4  demo::pick::<u8>
       1  demo::plain
  0 function(s) at or over complexity 10, 0 at or over CRAP 30
(dry run) would write coverage/cobertura.xml

```
